---
// Full HTML body for the IELTS Speaking post.
// Migrated from index.html — all CSS lives in src/styles/global.css.
---

<!-- HERO -->
<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-tag">IELTS Speaking 8.0 — Personal Training Kit</div>
  <h1 class="hero-title">Speak<br /><em>Native.</em></h1>
  <p class="hero-sub">A 6-week structured program to close the gap between correct English and <em>natural</em> English — built around the C.H.A.I.N. framework.</p>
  <div class="hero-meta">
    <div class="hero-stat">
      <div class="hero-stat-num">6</div>
      <div class="hero-stat-label">Weeks</div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-stat">
      <div class="hero-stat-num">60'</div>
      <div class="hero-stat-label">Per Day</div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-stat">
      <div class="hero-stat-num">8.0+</div>
      <div class="hero-stat-label">Target</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-scroll">Scroll to explore</div>
</section>

<!-- BAND COMPARE -->
<section class="section reveal">
  <div class="section-label">The Gap</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">From Band <em>7</em> to Band <em>8+</em></h2>
  <p class="section-desc">The jump isn't about more vocabulary or better grammar. It's about how answers feel — natural, layered, and effortlessly engaging.</p>

  <div class="band-compare">
    <div class="band-col">
      <div class="band-score">7.0</div>
      <div class="band-label">Current Level</div>
      <div class="band-trait">Answers are clear and correct</div>
      <div class="band-trait">Responds directly to the question</div>
      <div class="band-trait">Occasional pausing to find words</div>
      <div class="band-trait">Uses vocabulary accurately but simply</div>
      <div class="band-trait">Ideas stated but not expanded naturally</div>
    </div>
    <div class="band-arrow">→</div>
    <div class="band-col target">
      <div class="band-score">8.0+</div>
      <div class="band-label">Target</div>
      <div class="band-trait"><strong>Answers feel spontaneous and warm</strong></div>
      <div class="band-trait"><strong>Naturally hedges, expands, and pivots</strong></div>
      <div class="band-trait"><strong>Pausing is strategic, not desperate</strong></div>
      <div class="band-trait"><strong>Idiomatic chunks flow without effort</strong></div>
      <div class="band-trait"><strong>Ideas build on each other organically</strong></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FRAMEWORK -->
<section class="section reveal">
  <div class="section-label">The Framework</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">The <em>C.H.A.I.N.</em><br />Method</h2>
  <p class="section-desc">Five techniques that, when chained together, transform a textbook answer into a native-sounding response. Each letter is one learnable skill.</p>

  <div class="framework-grid">
    <div class="framework-card">
      <div class="fw-letter">C</div>
      <div class="fw-word">Chunk</div>
      <div class="fw-name">Ready-made Launchers & Chunks</div>
      <div class="fw-desc">Pre-loaded response openers and idiomatic phrases that bypass translation mode entirely. The first 3 words determine the whole answer's tone.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="framework-card">
      <div class="fw-letter">H</div>
      <div class="fw-word">Hedge</div>
      <div class="fw-name">Hedging & Nuance</div>
      <div class="fw-desc">Real people don't speak in absolutes. Adding "not exactly," "kind of," "I wouldn't say" makes answers feel human, not rehearsed.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="framework-card">
      <div class="fw-letter">A</div>
      <div class="fw-word">Anchor</div>
      <div class="fw-name">Anchor to Specifics</div>
      <div class="fw-desc">Replace abstract reasons ("it's fun") with concrete sensory details, memories, or images. Specifics create connection.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="framework-card">
      <div class="fw-letter">I</div>
      <div class="fw-word">Invite</div>
      <div class="fw-name">Invite the Listener</div>
      <div class="fw-desc">Hooks like "you know?", "right?", contrast structure, and self-deprecating humor pull the examiner into your answer.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="framework-card">
      <div class="fw-letter">N</div>
      <div class="fw-word">Navigate</div>
      <div class="fw-name">Navigate with Rhythm</div>
      <div class="fw-desc">Alternate short punchy sentences with longer flowing ones. End with impact. Rhythm is what separates fluent from native-sounding.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="example-box">
    <div class="example-label">C.H.A.I.N. in action — IELTS Part 1</div>
    <div class="example-q">Q: Do you enjoy listening to music?</div>
    <div class="example-a">
      <span class="highlight">C</span> "Oh, absolutely — it's genuinely one of my favorite things.
      <span class="highlight">H</span> I wouldn't call myself an audiophile or anything,
      <span class="highlight">A</span> but I'll randomly start humming in the middle of doing dishes and not even realize it.
      <span class="highlight">I</span> There's just something about it that shuts my brain off in a way nothing else really does, you know?
      <span class="highlight">N</span> It just works. Every single time."
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 6-WEEK ROADMAP -->
<section class="section reveal">
  <div class="section-label">The Plan</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">6-Week <em>Roadmap</em></h2>
  <p class="section-desc">One skill per week, building on the last. By week 6, all five C.H.A.I.N. elements fire automatically without conscious effort.</p>

  <div class="roadmap">
    <div class="week-row">
      <div class="week-num" style="background:var(--week1);">
        1
        <div class="week-label" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);">week</div>
      </div>
      <div class="week-content">
        <div class="week-title">Launchers & Chunks (C)</div>
        <div class="week-focus">Kill "Yes I do, I like X because..." forever. Build a bank of 20+ natural openers. Train until the first 3 words come out automatically before thinking.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="week-drill">
        <div class="week-drill-label">Daily Drill</div>
        <div class="week-drill-text">10 random questions → answer starting only with launchers. No "Yes/No" allowed. Record audio, review awkward moments.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="week-row">
      <div class="week-num" style="background:var(--week2);">
        2
        <div class="week-label" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);">week</div>
      </div>
      <div class="week-content">
        <div class="week-title">Hedging & Contrast (H + I partial)</div>
        <div class="week-focus">Add nuance to every answer. Nothing is 100% — practice "but," "except," "kind of," "not exactly." Add one self-deprecating line per answer.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="week-drill">
        <div class="week-drill-label">Daily Drill</div>
        <div class="week-drill-text">Take Week 1 answers → add hedge + contrast. Compare: does it sound more human? Shadow 1 native podcast clip/day.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="week-row">
      <div class="week-num" style="background:var(--week3);">
        3
        <div class="week-label" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);">week</div>
      </div>
      <div class="week-content">
        <div class="week-title">Anchoring to Specifics (A)</div>
        <div class="week-focus">Replace "it's relaxing / it's fun / I enjoy it" with one concrete sensory detail or memory per answer. Abstract → vivid.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="week-drill">
        <div class="week-drill-label">Daily Drill</div>
        <div class="week-drill-text">"Abstract Swap" game: write an abstract reason, convert to specific image. 10 rounds. Then use in speaking answers.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="week-row">
      <div class="week-num" style="background:var(--week4);">
        4
        <div class="week-label" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);">week</div>
      </div>
      <div class="week-content">
        <div class="week-title">Listener Hooks & Rhythm (I + N)</div>
        <div class="week-focus">Add "you know?", "right?", "I mean" as natural connectors. Practice rhythm: short sentence → long sentence → short impact ending.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="week-drill">
        <div class="week-drill-label">Daily Drill</div>
        <div class="week-drill-text">Read aloud 3 model native answers. Mark the rhythm pattern. Imitate. Record yourself and compare flow.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="week-row">
      <div class="week-num" style="background:var(--week5);">
        5
        <div class="week-label" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);">week</div>
      </div>
      <div class="week-content">
        <div class="week-title">Full C.H.A.I.N. Integration</div>
        <div class="week-focus">Combine all 5 elements consciously. Build 30 model answers across Part 1, 2, 3 topics. Focus on flow between elements, not perfection.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="week-drill">
        <div class="week-drill-label">Daily Drill</div>
        <div class="week-drill-text">Mock Part 1 (4 min) + Part 2 (2 min) + Part 3 (4 min). Record everything. Label which CHAIN elements you used.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="week-row">
      <div class="week-num" style="background:var(--week6);">
        6
        <div class="week-label" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);">week</div>
      </div>
      <div class="week-content">
        <div class="week-title">Automaticity & Mock Tests</div>
        <div class="week-focus">C.H.A.I.N. should be unconscious now. Full mock tests under timed conditions. Focus on naturalness, not technique. Review for remaining stiff patterns.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="week-drill">
        <div class="week-drill-label">Daily Drill</div>
        <div class="week-drill-text">Full 15-min mock test daily. Compare recordings from Week 1 vs now. Identify remaining gaps and target specifically.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- DAILY SCHEDULE -->
<section class="section reveal">
  <div class="section-label">Daily Structure</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">The <em>60-Minute</em> Session</h2>
  <p class="section-desc">Same structure every day. Consistency beats intensity. The order matters — warm up before performing, review before sleeping on it.</p>

  <div class="schedule-grid">
    <div class="schedule-block">
      <div class="schedule-time">10'</div>
      <div class="schedule-unit">minutes</div>
      <div class="schedule-name">Warm-Up: Shadowing</div>
      <div class="schedule-desc">Listen to 1 native clip (podcast, YouTube). Repeat immediately after, matching rhythm and intonation. Not about content — about feel.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="schedule-block" style="background:var(--warm)">
      <div class="schedule-time">15'</div>
      <div class="schedule-unit">minutes</div>
      <div class="schedule-name">Chunk Drilling</div>
      <div class="schedule-desc">Review and practice that week's target skill. Flashcard launchers, practice hedges, or do the abstract-swap game depending on the week.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="schedule-block">
      <div class="schedule-time">25'</div>
      <div class="schedule-unit">minutes</div>
      <div class="schedule-name">Speaking Practice</div>
      <div class="schedule-desc">Answer 8–10 IELTS questions aloud. Record audio. No stopping, no self-correcting mid-sentence. Flow matters more than accuracy here.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="schedule-block" style="background:var(--warm)">
      <div class="schedule-time">10'</div>
      <div class="schedule-unit">minutes</div>
      <div class="schedule-name">Review & Rebuild</div>
      <div class="schedule-desc">Listen back to recording. Pick 2–3 stiff or robotic moments. Rewrite and re-record those specific moments using C.H.A.I.N.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- TECHNIQUES QUICK REF -->
<section class="section reveal">
  <div class="section-label">Quick Reference</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">All <em>12 Techniques</em></h2>
  <p class="section-desc">The complete toolkit. Each technique is one learnable habit. Collect them one at a time.</p>

  <div class="techniques-list">
    <div class="technique-row">
      <div class="tech-num">1</div>
      <div class="tech-name">Launchers</div>
      <div class="tech-example">"Oh definitely..." / "Honestly, yeah..." / "Not really, to be honest..."</div>
    </div>
    <div class="technique-row">
      <div class="tech-num">2</div>
      <div class="tech-name">Hedging</div>
      <div class="tech-example">"I wouldn't call myself..." / "Not exactly, but..." / "Kind of, I guess..."</div>
    </div>
    <div class="technique-row">
      <div class="tech-num">3</div>
      <div class="tech-name">Anchoring</div>
      <div class="tech-example">"I'll just randomly start humming in the middle of doing dishes..."</div>
    </div>
    <div class="technique-row">
      <div class="tech-num">4</div>
      <div class="tech-name">Contrast Structure</div>
      <div class="tech-example">"I love hiking, but ask me to wake up at 5am for it and suddenly I'm not so sure"</div>
    </div>
    <div class="technique-row">
      <div class="tech-num">5</div>
      <div class="tech-name">Self-deprecating Humor</div>
      <div class="tech-example">"My neighbors probably hate me for it, but that's their problem"</div>
    </div>
    <div class="technique-row">
      <div class="tech-num">6</div>
      <div class="tech-name">Sensory Language</div>
      <div class="tech-example">"It just shuts my brain off" / "I lose track of time completely"</div>
    </div>
    <div class="technique-row">
      <div class="tech-num">7</div>
      <div class="tech-name">Listener Hooks</div>
      <div class="tech-example">"...you know?" / "...right?" / "I mean, it depends, but..."</div>
    </div>
    <div class="technique-row">
      <div class="tech-num">8</div>
      <div class="tech-name">Pivot Question</div>
      <div class="tech-example">"Anyway, what about you — are you into that kind of thing?"</div>
    </div>
    <div class="technique-row">
      <div class="tech-num">9</div>
      <div class="tech-name">Vague but Vivid</div>
      <div class="tech-example">"There's just something about it" / "It hits different when..."</div>
    </div>
    <div class="technique-row">
      <div class="tech-num">10</div>
      <div class="tech-name">Rhythm: Short + Long</div>
      <div class="tech-example">"It just works. Every single time." [short impact after long sentence]</div>
    </div>
    <div class="technique-row">
      <div class="tech-num">11</div>
      <div class="tech-name">Natural Intensifiers</div>
      <div class="tech-example">"so much fun" / "genuinely enjoy" / "I'm obsessed with" / "pretty solid"</div>
    </div>
    <div class="technique-row">
      <div class="tech-num">12</div>
      <div class="tech-name">Think-in-English Starters</div>
      <div class="tech-example">"The thing is..." / "What I love about it is..." / "It's one of those things where..."</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- DRILLS -->
<section class="section reveal">
  <div class="section-label">Exercises</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">Core <em>Drills</em></h2>
  <p class="section-desc">Six exercises that target the specific gaps: slow idea generation, straight answers, and chunk retrieval speed.</p>

  <div class="drills-grid">
    <div class="drill-card">
      <div class="drill-number">Drill 01</div>
      <div class="drill-name">Launcher Roulette</div>
      <div class="drill-time">10 min/day — Weeks 1–2</div>
      <div class="drill-desc">Builds automatic opener fluency. Kill the habit of starting with "Yes/No."</div>
      <ul class="drill-steps">
        <li>Draw a random IELTS Part 1 question</li>
        <li>Answer must start with a launcher — no exceptions</li>
        <li>Do 10 questions in a row, timed</li>
        <li>Goal: launcher comes out before conscious thought</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="drill-card">
      <div class="drill-number">Drill 02</div>
      <div class="drill-name">Abstract Swap</div>
      <div class="drill-time">10 min/day — Week 3</div>
      <div class="drill-desc">Trains the brain to instantly reach for specific images instead of generic reasons.</div>
      <ul class="drill-steps">
        <li>Write: "I like X because it's [abstract adjective]"</li>
        <li>Convert to: one specific image, moment, or sensation</li>
        <li>Do 10 swaps in writing first, then say them aloud</li>
        <li>Later: skip writing, go straight to speaking</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="drill-card">
      <div class="drill-number">Drill 03</div>
      <div class="drill-name">Shadow & Steal</div>
      <div class="drill-time">10 min/day — All 6 weeks</div>
      <div class="drill-desc">The most powerful input drill. Steals native rhythm, intonation, and chunking directly from real speakers.</div>
      <ul class="drill-steps">
        <li>Pick a 60-second podcast or YouTube clip</li>
        <li>Listen once without stopping</li>
        <li>Repeat immediately after, matching rhythm exactly</li>
        <li>Steal 1–2 phrases to use in today's practice</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="drill-card">
      <div class="drill-number">Drill 04</div>
      <div class="drill-name">The Rebuild</div>
      <div class="drill-time">10 min/day — All 6 weeks</div>
      <div class="drill-desc">Directly fixes the stiff and robotic moments by rewriting and re-recording them.</div>
      <ul class="drill-steps">
        <li>Listen back to today's recording</li>
        <li>Mark 2–3 moments that sound stiff or textbook-y</li>
        <li>Rewrite those sentences using C.H.A.I.N.</li>
        <li>Record those moments again and compare</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="drill-card">
      <div class="drill-number">Drill 05</div>
      <div class="drill-name">Contrast Challenge</div>
      <div class="drill-time">5 min/day — Week 2</div>
      <div class="drill-desc">Forces nuance into every answer. Kills overly positive or overly negative monotone responses.</div>
      <ul class="drill-steps">
        <li>Pick any topic you like or dislike</li>
        <li>Find one thing you like AND one thing you don't</li>
        <li>Build an answer using both — "I love X, but..."</li>
        <li>Add self-deprecating humor if possible</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="drill-card">
      <div class="drill-number">Drill 06</div>
      <div class="drill-name">Full Mock Simulation</div>
      <div class="drill-time">15 min/session — Weeks 5–6</div>
      <div class="drill-desc">The real test is pressure. Practice under time constraints so fluency holds under stress.</div>
      <ul class="drill-steps">
        <li>Set a timer. No pausing, no rewinding</li>
        <li>Part 1: 4 min (4 questions)</li>
        <li>Part 2: 2 min monologue on a cue card</li>
        <li>Part 3: 4 min (3–4 deeper questions)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- TIPS -->
<section class="section reveal">
  <div class="section-label">Teaching Notes</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">For the <em>Coach</em></h2>
  <p class="section-desc">How to make this program work as the person running sessions together.</p>

  <div class="tips-grid">
    <div class="tip-card">
      <div class="tip-icon">🎯</div>
      <div class="tip-title">One skill at a time</div>
      <div class="tip-desc">Don't teach all 12 techniques at once. Follow the weekly plan. Fluency is built layer by layer, not all at once.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tip-card">
      <div class="tip-icon">🎙️</div>
      <div class="tip-title">Record everything</div>
      <div class="tip-desc">Audio recording is non-negotiable. People can't hear themselves in real time. Playback reveals what coaching alone can't.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tip-card">
      <div class="tip-icon">⚡</div>
      <div class="tip-title">No mid-answer corrections</div>
      <div class="tip-desc">Let the answer finish before giving feedback. Interrupting breaks the flow habit you're trying to build.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tip-card">
      <div class="tip-icon">📺</div>
      <div class="tip-title">Input sources matter</div>
      <div class="tip-desc">Best sources: Conan O'Brien Needs a Friend, Diary of a CEO, Emma Chamberlain. Natural, unscripted, conversational English.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tip-card">
      <div class="tip-icon">🏆</div>
      <div class="tip-title">Celebrate natural moments</div>
      <div class="tip-desc">When something sounds genuinely native, mark it and repeat it. Positive reinforcement accelerates chunk acquisition faster than correcting errors.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="tip-card">
      <div class="tip-icon">🔁</div>
      <div class="tip-title">Repeat good answers</div>
      <div class="tip-desc">When a great answer comes out, say it again immediately. Repetition while the neural pattern is fresh burns it in faster.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
